  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math>Aluminium Chloride in acidified aqueous solution forms octahedral <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Al</mi><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> ion.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AlCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msup><mover><mrow><mover><mo>→</mo><mtext>Acidified aqueous solution</mtext></mover><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Al</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow></mrow></mover><mrow></mrow></msup></math></p><p>In this complex the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> orbital of Al are involved and the hybridisation state of Al is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p><p>Hence, the answer is option A.</p>"
